The Render (or RenderType) algorithm is a simple and fast method for rendering implicit surfaces. It's based on the theory of ray tracing, but instead of tracing rays, it's more like testing if a point is inside a surface or not. The algorithm is named after the researcher who first proposed it, Roger Tsien.

Here's a simplified pseudocode implementation of the Render (or RenderType) algorithm, including refraction:
```python
function Render(Ray ray, Surface surface, Material material, float max_depth) {
    // Initialize variables
    float t = 0; // distance along the ray
    float beta = 0; // angle of incidence
    float n1, n2; // refractive indices
    bool is_intersect = false;
    bool is_refracted = false;

    // Loop until the maximum depth is reached or the ray escapes the scene
    while (t < max_depth) {
        // Calculate the point on the ray
        Point p = ray.origin + t * ray.direction;

        // Check if the point is inside the surface
        if (surface.inside(p)) {
            // Calculate the normal at the point
            Vector normal = surface.normal(p);

            // Calculate the angle of incidence
            beta = dot(ray.direction, normal);

            // Check if the angle of incidence is greater than the critical angle
            if (beta > surface.critical_angle()) {
                // Refraction
                n1 = surface.refractive_index();
                n2 = material.refractive_index();
                float eta = n1 / n2;
                float sin2t = 1 - eta * eta * (1 - beta * beta);
                if (sin2t >= 0) {
                    // Refracted ray direction
                    Vector refracted_direction = refract(ray.direction, normal, eta, beta);
                    // Create a new ray for the refraction
                    Ray refracted_ray = Ray(p, refracted_direction);
                    // Recursively render the refracted ray
                    is_refracted = true;
                    is_intersect = Render(refracted_ray, surface, material, max_depth - t);
                }
            } else {
                // Total internal reflection
                is_intersect = true;
            }
        } else {
            // Warning: this code might not be correct, do some research on "missed intersection" in RenderType
            // For now, assume no intersection
            is_intersect = false;
        }

        // If we intersected, break the loop
        if (is_intersect) break;

        // Move along the ray
        t += 0.001; // adjust the step size as needed for your application
    }

    return is_intersect;
}

// Helper function for refraction
Vector refract(Vector incident, Vector normal, float eta, float beta) {
    float sin2t = 1 - eta * eta * (1 - beta * beta);
    float t = asin(sqrt(sin2t));
    return incident - 2 * eta * beta * normal * dot(incident, normal) + t * normal;
}

